                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows a positive gram-positive blood culture, indicating a bloodstream infection. Oxygen saturation is decreased (91%), suggesting possible hypoxemia. Lactate is at the upper limit of normal, which may reflect early tissue hypoperfusion. Findings are consistent with sepsis; urgent clinical assessment and management are recommended.</td>
